        <h2>Summary / Description</h2>
        <div class="description">
          Size measured from images after growth under LSMMG and normal gravity (NG). Treatment included LSMMG and NG in high-aspect ratio vessels (HARV) on rotating cell culture system (RCCS). For size determination LHM4 strain was used. This is a derivative of strain 1218R. TO produce LHM4 a plasmid was incorporated into the genome of 1218R. The plasmid encodes red fluorescent protein and kanamycin resistance. Bacteria were grown and experiments performed according to Abshire et al NPJ Microgravity (2016) 2, 16038; doi:10.1038/npjmgrav.2016.38.  
<p>
A portion of the LHM4 culture grown for 4 days in a 10 ml HARV was passed through a 27.5 gauge needle and fixed by the addition of 30 µl 4% paraformaldehyde to 10 µl of culture. Samples were placed at 4°C for at least 24 hrs prior to the measurement of the diameter and length of 50 bacteria using microscopy. The Instat3 program and the Unpaired T-test or the Mann-Whitney test was used to compare the lengths and diameters of the bacterium. 
<p>
Time period of collection November 2014.
        </div>

